// scene3d/motion/motion_command_full.js — bare low-16 → full 32-bit
// MotionCommand.
//
// Bugs 2 / 15 / 18 (2026-10-07). A MotionTable LINK is keyed
// `links[(style << 16) | (substate & 0xFFFFFF)][motion]` and the INNER key is
// the FULL 32-bit command (holtburger-dat motion_table.rs `get_link`; retail
// `CMotionTable::get_link`, acclient.c:337631). Remote motions reach JS as the
// wire's bare low-16 (`position.rs` `u32::from(motion_command_u16)`), and the
// local Ready alternated between bare 0x3 (setLocalStance) and full
// 0x41000003 (the input path). Every link lookup with a bare target missed;
// before bug 2's isLink check the wasm then baked the target's CYCLE in place
// of the missing link, and that full Ready/Run loop played as a one-shot in
// front of the real animation (the combat-stance "pop" before the draw, the
// late first monster swing, the delayed cast windup).
//
// Retail never sees a bare command: `MovementManager::unpack_movement`
// rebuilds the full value from the wire's command id (OpenAC
// `CombatAnimationPlanner.ReconstructFullCommand`). The low 16 bits are unique
// across all 408 non-zero commands of ACE's MotionCommand enum
// (Source/ACE.Entity/Enum/MotionCommand.cs, which also covers every
// MotionStance), so the lookup below is exact. Generated from that enum.

